    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-sample/q2",
      "question": "<p>Some A level students were given the following question.</p><p>Solve, for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-90^\\circ&lt;\\theta&lt;90^\\circ\"></span>, the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta=2\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The attempts of two of the students are shown below.</p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:60mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-sample/q02-figure.svg\" alt=\"Two boxed attempts. Student A: cos θ = 2 sin θ, tan θ = 2, θ = 63.4°. Student B: cos θ = 2 sin θ, cos² θ = 4 sin² θ, 1 − sin² θ = 4 sin² θ, sin² θ = 1/5, sin θ = ±1/√5, θ = ±26.6°.\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Identify an error made by student <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>Student <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=-26.6^\\circ\"></span> as one of the answers to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta=2\\sin\\theta\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Explain why this answer is incorrect.</li><li>Explain how this incorrect answer arose.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
