      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-sample/q6",
      "question": "<p>Complete the table below. The first one has been done for you.</p><p>For each statement you must state if it is always true, sometimes true or never true, giving a reason in each case.</p><table class=\"practice-table\"><tr><th>Statement</th><th>Always True</th><th>Sometimes True</th><th>Never True</th><th>Reason</th></tr><tr><td>The quadratic equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax^2+bx+c=0,\\quad(a\\neq0)\"></span> has 2 real roots.</td><td></td><td>✓</td><td></td><td>It only has 2 real roots when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^2-4ac&gt;0\"></span>. When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^2-4ac=0\"></span> it has 1 real root and when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^2-4ac&lt;0\"></span> it has 0 real roots.</td></tr><tr><td>(i)<br>When a real value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> is substituted into <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2-6x+10\"></span> the result is positive. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>(ii)<br>If <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax&gt;b\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;\\dfrac ba\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>(iii)<br>The difference between consecutive square numbers is odd. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>",
