      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\"><li>Express <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\cos\\theta-3\\sin\\theta\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\\cos(\\theta+\\alpha)\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R&gt;0\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;\\alpha&lt;90^\\circ\"></span><br>Give the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> and give the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span>, in degrees, to 2 decimal places. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:75mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-sample/q13-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3: a Ferris wheel beside a graph of H against t on a grid, showing two complete cycles of a wave starting near the t-axis\"></figure><p>The height above the ground, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\"></span> metres, of a passenger on a Ferris wheel <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> minutes after the wheel starts turning, is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"H=a-10\\cos(80t)^\\circ+3\\sin(80t)^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a constant.</p><p>Figure 3 shows the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\"></span> against <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> for two complete cycles of the wheel.</p><p>Given that the initial height of the passenger above the ground is 1 metre,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>find a complete equation for the model,</li><li>hence find the maximum height of the passenger above the ground.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Find the time taken, to the nearest second, for the passenger to reach the maximum height on the second cycle.<p>(<em>Solutions based entirely on graphical or numerical methods are 