      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-sample/q15",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:50mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-02-sample/q15-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 4: sketch of the curve C for x ≥ 0 and its tangent l at P; the shaded region R lies between C, l and the y-axis\"></figure><p>Figure 4 shows a sketch of the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=5x^{\\frac32}-9x+11,\\qquad x\\geqslant0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4, 15)\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>.</p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> is the tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>.</p><p>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 4, is bounded by the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis.</p><p>Show that the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is 24, making your method clear.</p><p>(<em>Solutions based entirely on graphical or numerical methods are not acceptable.</em>) <span class=\"marks\">(10)</span></p>",
