      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-02-sample/q16",
      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\"><li>Express <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{1}{P(11-2P)}\"></span> in partial fractions. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>A population of meerkats is being studied.</p><p>The population is modelled by the differential equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\mathrm dP}{\\mathrm dt}=\\frac1{22}P(11-2P),\\qquad t\\geqslant0,\\qquad 0&lt;P&lt;5.5\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, in thousands, is the population of meerkats and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> is the time measured in years since the study began.</p><p>Given that there were 1000 meerkats in the population when the study began,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>determine the time taken, in years, for this population of meerkats to double, <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li><li>show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"P=\\frac{A}{B+C\\mathrm e^{-\\frac12t}}\" data-display=\"true\"></div>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> are integers to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
